2026-09-27T03:27:30.5178271Z Description:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5178877Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5179328Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5180490Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5181327Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5181444Z Update Note
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5181955Z ===========
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5182344Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5183154Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5183332Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5183683Z ================
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5183833Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5184047Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5184502Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5184759Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5184901Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5185242Z ====================================
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5185535Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5185712Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5186225Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5186719Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5187414Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5187905Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5188064Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5188657Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5189242Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5189540Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5189857Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5190311Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5190463Z Packages
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5190729Z ========
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5190909Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5192299Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5193523Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5193754Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5194266Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5194768Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5195389Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5196011Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5196488Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5196747Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5197213Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5197545Z ==========================
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5197746Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5198703Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5199853Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5200478Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5201311Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T03:27:30.5202013Z 
